description: when code to be added/modified is part of a rust grpc microservice (Tonic)
alwaysApply: false
---
  You are an expert in Rust, gRPC (Tonic), and scalable microservice development. You give thoughtful and nuanced answers that are accurate and factual. You write bug-free, production ready code.

  Pair with: code-craft, rust-core, backend-usecases (when cross-domain orchestration applies), and monorepo rules for `protobuf/` + `backend/lib/gen/pb`. HTTP audience URL versioning (http-api-contract) does **not** apply — version gRPC via protobuf packages. Include `testing` when writing automated tests.

### Key Principles
  - Write concise, technical Rust code (see also code-craft and rust-core).
  - Organize by feature under `src/features/<name>/`, not by technical layer folders alone.
  - Within a feature, group by fixed file responsibilities (`endpoints.rs`, `service.rs`, `error.rs`, `config.rs`; add `repository.rs` when persistence is needed; add `dto.rs` / `entity.rs` when types outgrow the main files).
  - Do not invent layer subfolders under a feature (`handlers/`, `repositories/`, etc.). In particular, do **not** put a `services/` directory inside a feature module — feature logic stays in that feature’s `service.rs`. Shared domain modules live only at `src/services/<name>/`.
  - Package roles (do not conflate these):
    - `src/features/<name>/` — primary unit: transport + feature-owned domain logic
    - `src/services/<name>/` — shared application/domain services used by 2+ features (no gRPC registration here). Promote only after real reuse; do not put domain workflows in `common/`
    - `src/integrations/<name>/` — external systems (NATS, Cognito, etc.)
    - `src/database/` — SQL infra when needed
    - `src/common/` — dumb helpers only, extracted after real reuse
    - `src/usecases/<name>/` — optional; rare cross-domain orchestration RPCs (see backend-usecases)
  - Modules are crate-private by default; `pub` only when another module needs the item.
  - Feature-only adapters may start inside the feature and move to `integrations/` when they become service-wide.
  - Single-provider integrations may start with `client.rs` + `models.rs` only; add `<provider>.rs` when a second vendor/impl appears.
  - Define traits where they are used, not where they are implemented. Keep traits small and single-responsibility.
  - Always update aggregates through their aggregate root; do not mutate child entities from outside the root.
  - Features may be in-memory, messaging-backed, SQL-backed, or mixed — pick the persistence/integration that fits the domain.
  - Feature/usecase service entrypoints orchestrate by **calling** single-job helpers; do not inline separable multi-concern logic in the entrypoint (see code-craft Composition). Unit-test the helpers; cover the orchestrator with E2E/L2 (`testing.mdc`).
  - **Injectable seams:** **Collaborators required** (repos/integrations behind small traits; static generics per `rust-core`; wire at composition root). **Service-as-port is situational** (real second impl or cross-module consumer) — not for mocking services to unit-test handlers. ❌ Do not hold concrete integration types inside feature services.
  - Protobufs are the API contract: define services/messages in the monorepo `protobuf/` tree; consume generated Rust from the shared gen package (e.g. `backend/lib/gen/pb`). Do not hand-edit generated pb code.

### Rust/gRPC (Tonic)
  - Keep endpoints thin and push use-case logic into feature/shared services.
  - Use `rustfmt` and `clippy` when those tools are set up for the service.
  - Prefer sqlx for PostgreSQL when SQL is needed.
  - Prefer UUID v7 for IDs (see code-craft).
  - Time: `chrono` or `time` — pick one per service and stay consistent.
  - File structure (feature module approach):

```text
grpcserver/                          # e.g. backend/bserver (or domain name such as chatserver)
├── Cargo.toml
├── Dockerfile                       # Production build (prefer multi-stage)
├── .env.example                     # Optional but recommended
├── migrations/                      # Optional: sqlx migrate when SQL used — or under src/database/migrations/
├── docs/                            # Optional: service docs
├── tests/                           # Optional: integration / heavier tests
├── src/
│   ├── main.rs                      # Thin: load env → server::run
│   ├── bin/
│   │   └── client.rs                # Optional but recommended: developer CLI to exercise the service
│   ├── lib.rs                       # Optional: re-exports when useful for tests / client
│   ├── server/
│   │   ├── mod.rs
│   │   ├── app.rs                   # Tonic Server build, interceptors, lifecycle, service registration
│   │   └── state.rs                 # Optional shared deps
│   ├── client/                      # Optional: client library used by bin/client (and tests)
│   │   └── mod.rs
│   ├── environment/
│   │   └── mod.rs                   # Config from env (preferred over ad-hoc env in main)
│   ├── config/                      # Optional: richer multi-env loaders
│   │   └── mod.rs
│   ├── monitoring/                  # Optional: OTel / tracing helpers
│   │   └── mod.rs
│   ├── database/                    # Optional: SQL infra (only if DB used)
│   │   ├── mod.rs                   # Pool setup
│   │   ├── migrations/              # If not at service root
│   │   └── queries/                 # sqlx query modules / query files
│   ├── integrations/                # External-system adapters (only when needed)
│   │   └── <name>/                  # e.g. network/ (NATS), llm/, cognito/
│   │       ├── mod.rs
│   │       ├── client.rs            # Provider-agnostic trait + wiring
│   │       ├── <provider>.rs        # Optional until a second vendor appears
│   │       ├── models.rs            # DTOs / request-response types
│   │       └── client_test.rs       # Optional (or #[cfg(test)] in client.rs)
│   ├── services/                    # Shared app/domain (only after 2+ features need them)
│   │   └── <name>/                  # no tonic service registration here
│   │       ├── mod.rs
│   │       ├── service.rs           # Business rules / workflows
│   │       ├── models.rs            # Domain models / types
│   │       ├── repository.rs        # Optional: when this shared service owns persistence
│   │       └── service_test.rs      # Optional
│   ├── features/
│   │   └── <feature>/               # PRIMARY unit of organization
│   │       ├── mod.rs
│   │       ├── endpoints.rs         # tonic service impl
│   │       ├── service.rs           # Feature-owned logic; orchestrates repos/integrations/services
│   │       ├── service_test.rs      # Optional
│   │       ├── endpoints_test.rs    # Optional: unit tests for endpoint mapping
│   │       ├── repository.rs        # Optional: only if persistence is needed
│   │       ├── error.rs             # Domain / feature-level errors (thiserror)
│   │       ├── config.rs            # Feature-specific configuration (when needed)
│   │       ├── dto.rs               # Optional: split out when types grow
│   │       └── entity.rs            # Optional: split out when types grow
│   ├── usecases/                    # Optional: rare cross-domain orchestration (see backend-usecases)
│   │   └── <name>/
│   │       ├── mod.rs
│   │       ├── endpoints.rs         # tonic service impl for this product action
│   │       ├── service.rs           # Orchestrates features/services/integrations only
│   │       ├── error.rs
│   │       ├── dto.rs               # Optional
│   │       └── config.rs            # Optional
│   └── common/                      # Dumb helpers only — after real reuse
│       ├── mod.rs
